# WHERE THIS GOES depends on what you put in it.
#
#   the API KEY  ->  ~/.config/autosound/critic-env     (Windows: %APPDATA%\autosound\critic-env)
#   everything else -> rew_analitic/.critic-env in the project, if you want it per-car
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/autosound && cp scripts/.critic-env.example ~/.config/autosound/critic-env
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/autosound/critic-env
#
# And do NOT `export GEMINI_API_KEY` from ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc. A file is read by whoever knows
# its path; an exported variable is handed to EVERY process you start -- every npm package, every
# agent, every `env`. The wrappers export it themselves for the length of their own run, which is
# as long as it needs to exist.
#
# The key stays out of the project because the project folder is the one the README suggests
# backing up to a private GitHub. Both files are read, the machine one first, so an existing
# project-local file keeps working exactly as before.
#
# READ as KEY=VALUE, never executed: a line containing $( , a backtick or ; is dropped with a
# message. Quotes around a value are optional and stripped; they cost nothing and read clearer.

# A copy of this file WITH a key in it must be ignored by git wherever it lands (.critic-env is
# in the skill's and every seeded project's .gitignore) -- the wrappers refuse to read one that
# git would take, and scripts/secret-scan.py checks the tree. Best: keep the key in the machine
# file (~/.config/autosound/critic-env) and only models/paths in a project copy.
# ---- Default: real Antigravity (agy) ----
GEMINI_BIN=agy
# ONE reviewer, ONE model (the Arbiter's ruling, 2026-09-11 -- the Critic and the Advisor are one
# role). There used to be a second line here, GEMINI_ADVISOR_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-medium: agy
# stopped offering that whole generation, and the wrappers no longer read the variable at all.
# The scripts name NO model: unset, they print `agy models` and stop for you to pick. So the line
# below is an example to check, not a default -- run `agy models` and take a Pro `-high` id from
# its LEFT column (the display labels, "Gemini 3.1 Pro (High)", are rejected by agy >= 1.1.12).
GEMINI_CRITIC_MODEL=gemini-3.1-pro-high
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=<id>   # only if you want a weaker model tried when the quota is dry

# ---- The direct API with a KEY (autosound_ai.py; cross-platform, no CLI) ----
# @google/gemini-cli is CLOSED (2026-09-08, IneligibleTierError: "This client is no longer
# supported for Gemini Code Assist for individuals … migrate to the Antigravity suite") and a key
# in the environment did NOT reopen it (probed the same day) — do not pin GEMINI_BIN=gemini.
# A key still drives the direct API. Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — the current
# shape is AQ.… (53 chars); an AIza… (39) key is the old shape and answers API_KEY_INVALID once a
# new one exists. Keep the key in THIS file (per machine), not in a shell export: a session's
# environment does not follow ~/.zshrc after it started, and an export reaches every process.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AQ....
# AUTOSOUND_CRITIC_MODEL=gemini-pro-latest     # Google's own pointer to the current Pro. A dated id
#                                              # (gemini-2.5-*) retires under you: 404 on 2026-09-08.
#                                              # The script prints the key's list and stops when a
#                                              # pin is gone.

# PROJECT_MIRROR=/abs/path/to/project/rew_analitic   # only if CWD differs from the project
